### Slide 3: Executive Summary: Findings Breakdown
- **Audit Scoring & Category Matrix:**
  - *1. Quality Management System (IATF 16949 / ISO 26262):* PASS (100%)
  - *2. Design & Change Management (Rev B ECO):* PASS (100%)
  - *3. Problem Solving & 8D Execution (CAR-2024-ND01):* **EXEMPLARY PASS**
  - *4. Reliability Qualification (AEC-Q100 Data):* PASS (100%)
  - *5. Manufacturing & Fab SPC Controls:* PASS (98% — Minor Observation)
  - *6. Calibration & Metrology Lab Controls:* PASS (97% — Minor Observation)
- **Overall Compliance Score: 98.4% (Grade A Supplier Status).**
- *Speaker Notes:* "Klaus Meyer commended our 8D report as one of the most thorough root-cause investigations NovaDrive has reviewed this year."

---

### Slide 4: Review of 8D Corrective Action & Rev B Qual Data
- **Key Customer Audit Review Highlights:**
  - *Root Cause Transparency:* Rosa Santos presented the FIB cross-sections demonstrating the 120µm vs 280µm ESD clamp gate oxide breakdown. NovaDrive validated our technical findings.
  - *Permanent Corrective Action (PCA):* Verified CAD DRC rule implementation prohibiting commercial clamp macros in automotive projects.
  - *Rev B Reliability Retest:* Kevin Tran presented 1000-hour HTOL, TC, and HAST datasets with zero failures across 231 units.
  - *Yield Recovery:* James Ortiz demonstrated wafer probe yield increase from 41.2% to 82.1%.
- *Speaker Notes:* "NovaDrive specifically noted that our physical data left no room for skepticism. The transition to Rev B was validated in every detail."

---

### Slide 5: Minor Observations & Immediate Corrective Actions
- **Observation 1: Lab Test Equipment Calibration Sticker**
  - *Finding:* A secondary digital multimeter in Reliability Lab C had an expired calibration sticker (expired 5 days prior).
  - *Immediate Action:* Multimeter quarantined immediately; verified it was not used for qualification data recording; recalibrated and tagged by certified metrology vendor.
- **Observation 2: ESD Refresher Training Documentation**
  - *Finding:* Two newly onboarded junior technicians had not completed their formal annual ESD handling refresher record in the HR database.
  - *Immediate Action:* Technicians completed certified online refresher training module on-site during the audit afternoon; records archived.
- *Speaker Notes:* "Both minor observations were resolved before the closing meeting. Klaus Meyer closed both items on-site."

---

### Slide 6: Production Approval & Mass Production Next Steps
- **Commercial & Operational Release:**
  - NovaDrive signed the formal **Part Submission Warrant (PSW)** for Volta-7 Rev B silicon.
  - Production purchase orders released for initial volume: 150,000 units in June 2024, ramping to 250,000 units/month by Q4 2024.
  - FastChip authorized Penang Fab 2 to ramp wafer starts to 800 wafers/month.
- **Final Message:**
  - Volta-7 is officially transitioning from NPI development to High-Volume Production.
- *Speaker Notes:* "Congratulations to the entire Product Engineering team. We navigated an existential customer crisis and emerged as a top-tier automotive partner."
